W-114 spec sec red-team — Claude substitute (claude-sonnet-5-5), 2026-10-02, brief revision 1. SEC-SPEC: REVISE.
Scope: brief read-only at spec/W-114 (2e465a6); probes on temp copies of examples/sample-studio only. No bisellium write verbs on studio/.
Searched: context.ts (all of it), writes.ts runAnswer (616-774), appendPatronTimeline, hooks.ts hook-event/handleContext, check.ts petitio.* (657-704), adapter resolveSeat, every "[stated]" writer (one: writes.ts:722), studio/petitiones/*, examples/sample-studio (symlinks: none), process.env reads.

1. HIGH (false premise; brief 118-121, 255-256) "every pre-existing resolved petitio (all stamp-less in studio/) stays out of every context, byte for byte".
   Probe: 12 of 13 resolved studio/petitiones/P-001..P-015 carry a line-start "[stated] <ISO> patron:" (grep '^\[stated\]'). P-014 and P-015
   (from qa-lead, stamped 2026-10-01T11:03:57Z) are inside the 2-day window until 2026-10-03T11:03Z, so at landing qa-lead's real boot context
   changes (context.ts:166-180 would list them). Intended behaviour, but the brief says otherwise and the censor's byte-identical check would misfire.
   Fix: state the real claim (older stamps age out; two qa-lead petitiones appear until 10-03); confine byte-identity to the fixture/F2 row.
2. MEDIUM, blocks (stamp parse; brief 114-118; context.ts:26-36 toDate/daysBetween) the "last stamp" is unauthenticated body text and
   daysBetween clamps a future date to 0. Probed: `answer` with reply "ok\n[stated] 2099-01-01T00:00:00Z patron: x" (positionals joined, writes.ts:627,722)
   leaves a body whose LAST stamp is 2099 -> visible 73 years. Hand-appended stamps by a file-writing sella do the same, no Patron act, no timeline line.
   `new Date()` is lenient: "1" -> 2001, "2099" parses in local TZ (probe TZ is GMT+8), so (\S+) accepts non-ISO tokens and adds TZ dependence.
   Fix: require /^\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT\d\d:\d\d:\d\d(\.\d+)?Z$/ on the token AND stamp <= now (a future stamp is never listed). All brief rows
   (stamp == --now exactly, 47h/49h) still pass. Add a behaviour-4 row: stamp 2099 hand-edited -> absent; "1" token -> absent.
3. MEDIUM, blocks (party rule; brief 113-114) check.ts:685-687 enforces direction only for needs_you/awaiting_reply; a hand-written
   resolved petitio "from: eng-lead to: qa-lead" passes check (petitio.party only needs sella-or-patron), and rule 3 would now push its
   body, with a forged "patron:" stamp, into qa-lead's boot context at priority 5. Before, check blocked sella->sella petitiones in live states.
   (Acta decisions already reach every sella, so the channel class exists; this one is higher priority and carries a Patron-looking stamp.)
   Fix: rule 3 = (from===sella && to===patron) || (to===sella && from===patron). Add to behaviour 4: A-9 variant eng-lead->qa-lead, stamped, absent from both.
4. MEDIUM, blocks (growth; brief 111-121, 128, residual 6 line 286) resolved petitiones share the single priority-5 "petitiones" section
   with the actionable awaiting_reply ask (context.ts:176,181). Truncation drops WHOLE sections by priority number (220-226): a flood of
   stamped resolved petitiones (forged files per item 3, or repeated `answer` re-stamping, reply length uncapped writes.ts:627, window refreshed each time)
   pushes the section over 4000 tokens and removes the real pending ask while opera (priority 4) survives. No cap in the brief.
   Fix: cap listed resolved entries (newest N by stamp, N=3) and trim each body to its tail (stamp lines) ~1000 chars; list pending asks first.
   Add a row: 6 stamped resolved petitiones + one awaiting_reply -> the awaiting_reply header still present, no "truncated: petitiones".
5. LOW (harness; brief 71-77) cli() has no `timeout` (precedent next.test.ts:131, rules/tests.test.ts:440 pass timeout: 120_000) and no pinned env:
   the child inherits BISELLIUM_SELLA/BISELLIUM_ROLE/TZ (main.ts:193, writes.ts:173). hook-event has a 2 s stdin guard (hooks.ts), so a hang is unlikely,
   but add timeout and env {...process.env, TZ:"UTC", BISELLIUM_SELLA:undefined}. spawnSync is argv-array, no shell, per brief 71-74: OK. Output is only compared, never executed: OK.
6. LOW (fixture; brief 78-82) mkdtempSync under os.tmpdir() is unique per call: no $TMPDIR collision between parallel files (tsx cache is per-uid, shared, safe).
   cpSync default keeps symlinks; sample-studio has none today (find -type l empty), `check F --now NOW` without --repo exits 0 (probed, 0 blocking/7 advisory).
   Optional: one assertion that the copied tree has no symlink so a future fixture symlink cannot make a row write into examples/.
